{"name":"Biro Blue","hex":"#2f3946","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"biro","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Biro brand ballpoint pen.","Any ballpoint pen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biro"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballpoint pen","blocks":[{"text":"A ballpoint pen is a pen that dispenses ink over a hard ball rolling in its point. The materials commonly used are steel, brass, or tungsten carbide. The design was conceived and developed as a cleaner and more reliable alternative to dip pens and fountain pens. It is now the world's most-used writing instrument, with millions manufactured and sold daily. It has influenced art and graphic design and spawned an artwork genre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/03-BICcristal2008-03-26.jpg/330px-03-BICcristal2008-03-26.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballpoint_pen","wikidata":"Q160137"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/US392046-0.png/500px-US392046-0.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/US392046-0.png/1280px-US392046-0.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/US392046-0.png/500px-US392046-0.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Loud's patent of the ballpoint pen (1888)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS392046-0.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Bol%C3%ADgrafo_birome_II_edit.jpg/500px-Bol%C3%ADgrafo_birome_II_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Bol%C3%ADgrafo_birome_II_edit.jpg/500px-Bol%C3%ADgrafo_birome_II_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABol%C3%ADgrafo_birome_II_edit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Bol%C3%ADgrafo_marca_birome_I.jpg/500px-Bol%C3%ADgrafo_marca_birome_I.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Bol%C3%ADgrafo_marca_birome_I.jpg/1280px-Bol%C3%ADgrafo_marca_birome_I.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe